# roughness_knobs.mac — THE roughness settings of the pTP film, in one place.
#
# Applied by every macro when the simulation is started with rough=on
# (main.sh: ROUGH=on, which defines the macro alias {ROUGH} = 1), and ALWAYS
# by vis_roughness.mac. With rough=off nothing here is applied and the film
# stays exactly as configured in the YAML (pTPsigmaAlpha_rad, pTPgeomRough*).
#
# 1) PHYSICS roughness — this is what the production runs use (run.mac,
#    run_vuv_spectrum.mac, run_285.mac): RMS slope of the micro-facets of both
#    pTP faces [rad], Geant4 UNIFIED surface model. Invisible in the geometry,
#    it acts on the photon directions at the film surfaces (0 = perfectly
#    smooth, 0.1 rad ≈ 6°). Placeholder value — tune it to the measurement.
/detector/pTPsigmaAlpha 0.1
#
# 2) VISUAL exaggeration — only for vis_roughness.mac and draw_offscreen.mac,
#    which set the alias {ROUGHDEMO} = 1 before executing this file
#    (sim_lighttrap defines {ROUGHDEMO} = 0, so the production runs skip these
#    three lines): a 1 mm thick film with a random height map, so that the
#    bumps can be SEEN in the viewer. Real film: 0.002 mm, invisible.
/control/doif {ROUGHDEMO} == 1 /detector/pTPlayerthickness 1.0
/control/doif {ROUGHDEMO} == 1 /detector/pTPgeomRoughCells 30
/control/doif {ROUGHDEMO} == 1 /detector/pTPgeomRoughAmp 0.3
# (bumps per side: lateral bump size = 150 mm / 30 = 5 mm; RMS bump height in mm,
#  clipped at ±3 RMS and at 0.8 × film thickness)
/run/reinitializeGeometry
/run/initialize
